fluorine-artwork (0.5.0) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Add four 3840x2160 lossless PNG wallpapers under
    /usr/share/backgrounds/fluorine: grid, hex, topo, and void.
  * Render the wallpapers from committed SVG sources during the package build
    through tools/generate-wallpapers.sh, so the repository stays vector-only
    and every build produces byte-identical images.
  * Depend on librsvg2-bin at build time for rsvg-convert.

 -- gowthvm <gowthamgkofficial@gmail.com>  Wed, 25 Nov 2026 03:10:00 +0530

fluorine-artwork (0.4.0) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Replace the Plymouth theme with a rewritten fluorine theme. The previous
    script called Image.NewSolidColor and Image.NewGradient, neither of which
    exists in Plymouth 24.004.60, so the theme aborted at load and every boot
    fell back to the text splash.
  * Ship the hexagonal F emblem and the 2px progress bar as committed PNGs and
    crop the fill at runtime, which is the only solid-surface primitive the
    script plugin actually provides.
  * Draw the passphrase dialog as a muted label over a lime underline that grows
    with the typed passphrase, with no password echo and no boot log text.
  * Add a GRUB2 theme: black canvas, carbon entry panels inside a 2px hairline
    frame, and a lime frame on the selected entry.
  * Register fluorine as the default Plymouth theme and stage the GRUB theme
    under /boot/grub/themes from postinst.

 -- gowthvm <gowthamgkofficial@gmail.com>  Wed, 25 Nov 2026 01:10:00 +0530

fluorine-artwork (0.3.3) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Fix the void wallpaper: the octahedron geometry comment used a double hyphen,
    which is not legal inside an XML comment, so the file failed to parse and the
    wallpaper rendered blank in every theme that loads it.

